generatedCommentsNodes.comment:
**Bug: write position is advanced and `true` is returned even when the write fails.** The `WROTE_POSITION_UPDATER.addAndGet(...)` and `return true` sit *outside* the `try-catch`. If `fileChannel.position(...)` or `fileChannel.write(...)` throws, the code still advances the write offset and reports success to the caller. Subsequent appends will then skip over the unwritten region, silently corrupting the consume queue. Move both statements inside the `try` block (after a successful write) and return `false` in the `catch` path:
```java
@Override
public boolean appendMessageUsingFileChannel(byte[] data) {
    int currentPos = WROTE_POSITION_UPDATER.get(this);
    if ((currentPos + data.length) <= this.fileSize) {
        try {
            this.fileChannel.position(currentPos);
            this.fileChannel.write(ByteBuffer.wrap(data, 0, data.length));
            WROTE_POSITION_UPDATER.addAndGet(this, data.length);
            return true;
        } catch (Throwable e) {
            log.error("Error occurred when append message to mappedFile.", e);
            return false;
        }
    }
    return false;
}
```

